and one IP"},"301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use different external ports"},"302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Clients must include non-standard ports"},"303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate TLS/mTLS termination behind one IP"},"304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Front-door SNI routing to internal Gateways"},"305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Advanced design; the front door uses TLS passthrough and each internal Gateway terminates its own TLS"},"306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Separate Gateway resources but shared proxy infrastructure"},"307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy merged-Gateway mode"},"308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Logical separation only; listeners must have unique port, protocol and hostname tuples"},"309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Three independent `LoadBalancer` Services cannot all reserve the same node ports 80 and 443 through K3s ServiceLB. Use one shared Gateway, allocate distinct VIPs with another load-balancer implementation, or use different ports."},"310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Envoy Gateway normally provisions a proxy fleet per `Gateway`. Its merged-Gateway mode can share one fleet and address, but it is not a drop-in switch for multiple Lamassu releases: the generated Lamassu listeners use the same ports and protocols without distinct hostnames, so they conflict unless you deliberately customize the listener design."},"311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"Use a front-door SNI design only when the internal Gateways must retain independent TLS or mTLS policy:"},"312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#what-if-you-need-three-gateways","content":"This requires distinct SNI hostnames and cluster networking outside the Lamassu chart."},"313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If one Gateway can own TLS and routing, use the chart default."},"314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If Gateways need independent policy and you can allocate IPs, use one VIP per Gateway."},"315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If only the Kubernetes resources need separation, evaluate merged-Gateway mode and make every listener tuple unique."},"316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If data planes and TLS termination must stay independent behind one IP, add a front-door SNI passthrough layer."},"317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#decision-guide","content":"If none of those are possible, use different external ports or change the external network design."},"318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#egress-proxy","content":"Internal Lamassu clients — the Vault engine connection, service-to-service calls and webhook deliveries — honor the `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` and `NO_PROXY` environment variables. The exception is the authorization-engine connector: it uses its own transport and does not consult these proxy variables. If your deployment routes egress through a proxy, list in-cluster service names in `NO_PROXY` (for example `.svc,.cluster.local`) so internal traffic stays inside the cluster. Loopback traffic is never sent through a proxy."},"319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#egress-proxy","content":"The default transport of these clients bounds the dial timeout (30 seconds), the TLS handshake (10 seconds) and idle connection reuse (90 seconds) so an unreachable dependency fails fast instead of hanging; these values are Go transport defaults, not Lamassu settings. HTTP/2 is negotiated when the peer supports it. The authorization-engine connector keeps its own transport without these dial and handshake timeouts; only its overall 30-second request timeout bounds each call."},"320":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Check, in order:"},"321":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"`Gateway` has `Accepted=True` and `Programmed=True`."},"322":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Its status contains the expected address."},"323":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The generated `LoadBalancer` Service has a usable external address."},"324":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"Port 443 reaches that address from the client network."},"325":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"DNS resolves to the externally reachable endpoint."},"326":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The certificate contains the DNS name or IP used by the client."},"327":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/networking#verify-the-traffic-path","content":"The Gateway API treats addresses as desired state that a controller may assign or reject; see the Gateway API overview for the resource model."},"328":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"page","content":"Kubernetes self-managed","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment","Kubernetes self-managed"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview"},"329":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","content":"Choose an installation workflow and network architecture for Lamassu on your Kubernetes cluster."},"330":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview#self-managed-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Self-managed Kubernetes deployment"},"331":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview#choose-an-installation-workflow","content":"Choose an installation workflow"},"332":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-43/deployment/self-hosted/overview#what-the-lamassu-